.TH geectl-build-build-log 1  "geectl-build-build-log 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-build\-log \- Read the build log for a package
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build build\-log\fR [\fB\-\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-last\fR] [\fB\-\-lastsucceeded\fR] [\fB\-\-multibuild\fR] [\fB\-\-strip\-time\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> [\fIPACKAGE\fR] [\fIREPOSITORY\fR] [\fIARCH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the build log for a package
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fI<START>\fR
Start reading at this byte offset; a negative offset reads from the end of the log
.TP
\fB\-\-last\fR
The last build\*(Aqs log instead of the current one. Cannot combine with `\-\-lastsucceeded`
.TP
\fB\-\-lastsucceeded\fR
The last succeeded build\*(Aqs log. Cannot combine with `\-\-last`
.TP
\fB\-\-multibuild\fR \fI<FLAVOR>\fR
Only this multibuild flavor\*(Aqs log: appends `:FLAVOR` to the package. Refused when the package already carries a flavor
.TP
\fB\-\-strip\-time\fR
Strip the leading `[timestamp] ` from each log line
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in — or a build\-log URL, in which case the other coordinates are omitted. The URL form takes an API log URL (`http(s)://<api\-host>/build/<project>/<repository>/<arch>/<package>/_log`) or a web\-UI log URL (`http(s)://build.opensuse.org/package/live_build_log/<project>/<package>/<repository>/<arch>`)
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The package to read the log for. Omit with a URL
.TP
[\fIREPOSITORY\fR]
The repository the package builds in. Omit with a URL
.TP
[\fIARCH\fR]
The architecture the package builds for. Omit with a URL
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
